//? Title: The Luhn decimal check digit
//? Subtitle: Actual parity transformations, exhaustive original error controls and complete input contracts
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Luhn appends a decimal digit so an alternating weighted digit sum is zero modulo
ten. We retain the original7992739871 example and exhaustive single-error study,
expose the actual right-to-left transformations, and derive why all single
substitutions are caught while09/90 adjacent swaps can be missed.
)

\toc

> Tiny hand calculation: append five to twelve

Define t(d)=2*d for d<5 and2*d−9 otherwise. In a full string the rightmost digit
has weight one, its predecessor uses t, and the choices alternate moving left.
For a payload awaiting its appended check digit, its own rightmost digit must
use t: appending the new weight-one digit leaves those payload transformations
unchanged.

For payload12, its contributions are1 and4, sum5, so the appended digit is5. The
full string125 has contributions1,4,5 and weighted residue zero. The actual
capture visits indices2,1,0; the diagram uses those actual committed residues
and contributions. It does not repeat the checksum in the report.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/luhn_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = dm::algorithms::luhn_trace("125");
    std::print("| actual original index | actual digit | double | actual raw value | subtract nine | actual " "contribution | prior residue | actual next residue |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | " "---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index,
                   s.digit, s.doubled, s.raw, s.reduced, s.contribution,
                   s.before, s.after);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < t.steps.size(); ++i) {
        auto &s = t.steps[i];
        d.node(std::to_string(i), {6. * i, 0},
               std::format("Actual index{} digit{}\ncontribution{}, residue{}",
                           s.index, s.digit, s.contribution, s.after));
        if (i)
            d.edge(std::to_string(i - 1), std::to_string(i));
    }
    d.save_svg("build/luhn_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual original index | actual digit | double | actual raw value | subtract nine | actual contribution | prior residue | actual next residue |
| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 2 | 5 | false | 5 | false | 5 | 0 | 5 |
| 1 | 2 | true | 4 | false | 4 | 5 | 9 |
| 0 | 1 | false | 1 | false | 1 | 9 | 0 |
\image(figures/luhn_tiny.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Actual right-to-left checksum execution for125.)
\alttext(Three real producing steps show contributions5,4,1 and their bounded modular residues, ending at zero.)

> Original payload and full-number example

Retain payload7992739871 and full string79927398713. The native payload result
returns check digit3; the full-mode trace validates the appended string and
exposes every actual transformed contribution. The original79927398710 checksum
failure is retained separately. Leading zeros are never dropped by integer
parsing because the API consumes the exact decimal byte string.

Only residue modulo ten is required, so every producing update
stores(before+contribution)%10 with both terms bounded by nine. This avoids the
old unbounded signed-int sum for very long strings without changing any
well-formed nonempty checksum decision. Input validation checks every byte
before the first arithmetic step.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/luhn_original.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto payload =
        dm::algorithms::luhn_analyze("7992739871",
                                     dm::algorithms::LuhnMode::Payload);
    auto t = dm::algorithms::luhn_trace("79927398713");
    std::print("Actual generated digit {}; actual full validity {}; actual altered check-digit validity " "{}.\n\n| actual original index | actual digit | actual contribution | doubled | actual " "residue after this right-to-left step |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n",
               payload.check_digit, t.analysis.valid,
               dm::algorithms::luhn_validate("79927398710"));
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    for (auto &s : t.steps) {
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index, s.digit,
                   s.contribution, s.doubled, s.after);
        x.push_back(s.index);
        y.push_back(s.digit);
        z.push_back(s.contribution);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, y, "actual digits", {100, 116, 139}, 5).points(x, z,
                                                               "contributions",
                                                               {37, 99, 235}, 7).y_limits(-.5, 12).title("Original79927398713: actual transformed contributions").x_label("original decimal byte index").y_label("digit or actual transformed contribution").save_svg("build/luhn_original.svg");
}
```
