> Why single substitutions are detected, and the blind adjacent pair

At either parity, the digit-to-contribution map is a permutation modulo ten:
identity maps0..9 to0..9, and t maps them to0,2,4,6,8,1,3,5,7,9. Replacing one
digit by a distinct digit changes its contribution by a nonzero residue, so
every single substitution is detected, including a changed check digit.

For adjacent digits a,b with opposite parities, swapping them changes the
weighted sum by[t(a)−a]−[t(b)−b], up to sign. The ten values of t(d)−d modulo
ten are0,1,2,3,4,6,7,8,9,0. Only0 and9 share a value, so distinct adjacent
transpositions are detected except09/90. Equal adjacent digits are unchanged
strings, not errors, and the exhaustive study excludes them.

Retain the original payload1230904560907, append its native generated digit,
then let the native study construct and independently check all9*n single
substitutions and each distinct adjacent swap. The reported rates are exact
exhaustive counts for this prescribed string, not population error
probabilities. The table below preserves every actual missed case.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/luhn_detection.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto s = dm::algorithms::luhn_error_study("1230904560907");
    std::print("Actual complete original string {}.\n\n| actual error category | actual generated errors | " "actual detected | exact detected fraction |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| substitution | " "{} | {} | {} |\n| distinct adjacent swap | {} | {} | {} |\n\n| actual missed " "kind0:substitution,1:swap | actual changed index | actual changed string | actual residue " "|\n| ---: | ---: | --- | ---: |\n",
               s.full, s.substitutions, s.substitutions_detected,
               double(s.substitutions_detected) / s.substitutions, s.swaps,
               s.swaps_detected, double(s.swaps_detected) / s.swaps);
    for (auto &e : s.cases)
        if (!e.detected)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", int(e.kind), e.index,
                       e.changed, e.remainder);
    auto p =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::barplot({100. * s.substitutions_detected /
                                      s.substitutions,
                                      100. * s.swaps_detected / s.swaps},
                                     {"single substitution",
                                      "unequal adjacent swap"},
                                     "detected percent", {37, 99, 235});
    p.x_label("error category").y_label("exact exhaustive detection percent");
    p.title("Original prescribed string: exact single-error detection").y_limits(0, 120).save_svg("build/luhn_detection.svg");
}
```
