> Payload parity, empty strings and decimal validation

The payload mode and full mode have different rightmost parity, but appending
the generated check digit makes each original payload position retain precisely
its payload-mode transformation. The next figure/table compare the actual native
traces at matching original indices; the extra final check digit is represented
separately. This is a direct parity check, not an alternative checksum
implementation.

Inputs are ASCII decimal bytes only, including leading zeros. Signs, separators,
NULs, arbitrary high bytes and non-ASCII numerals throw invalid_argument after
complete validation; they are not silently stripped or treated as digits. Empty
payload is explicitly permitted and generates digit zero, so the nonempty full
string0 has residue zero. Empty full input now returns false rather than the
earlier accidental zero-sum true. A well-formed checksum failure returns false.
Checksum validity alone supplies no issued-identifier length/prefix/business
validation.

Ordinary checksum evaluation uses O(n) time and constant auxiliary storage. A
complete trace admits2*n logical original bytes and digit records before copies,
with default million cap and zero disabling only the optional cap. It excludes
fields, capacities, analysis/runtime copies and physical byte size. The
exhaustive error study owns every changed string and performs O(n*n) checksum
work/output bytes for full length n; its separate complete logical quota counts
payload/full bytes plus each error record and its changed bytes before error
copies. Captures own their strings and do not replay earlier prefixes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/luhn_parity.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const std::string payload = "7992739871";
    auto a =
        dm::algorithms::luhn_trace(payload, dm::algorithms::LuhnMode::Payload);
    const auto full = payload + char('0' + a.analysis.check_digit);
    auto b = dm::algorithms::luhn_trace(full);
    std::vector<double> x, y, z;
    std::print("| original payload index | actual payload contribution | actual full contribution at same " "index | actual equality |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (auto &s : a.steps) {
        const auto &other = b.steps[b.steps.size() - 1 - s.index];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.index, s.contribution,
                   other.contribution, s.contribution == other.contribution);
        x.push_back(s.index);
        y.push_back(s.contribution);
        z.push_back(other.contribution);
    }
    std::print("\nActual empty payload digit {}; empty full validity {}; leading-zero full validity {}; " "appended check digit {}.\n",
               dm::algorithms::luhn_check_digit(""),
               dm::algorithms::luhn_validate(""),
               dm::algorithms::luhn_validate("0000"), a.analysis.check_digit);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, y, "payload mode", {220, 38, 38}, 2).points(x, z, "full mode",
                                                          {37, 99, 235}, 5).y_limits(-.5, 12).title("Actual payload contributions survive check-digit append").x_label("original payload index").y_label("actual native transformed contribution").save_svg("build/luhn_parity.svg");
}
```
